# Critical workflow

- For every coding task, read and apply the global `code-quality` skill at `~/.agents/skills/code-quality/SKILL.md` before working on code.
- Prefer project-native tooling over ad-hoc commands.
- Before running JS/TS commands, detect the package manager from lockfiles (`pnpm-lock.yaml`, `package-lock.json`, `yarn.lock`, `bun.lockb`, `bun.lock`) and use that manager consistently.
- Prefer `package.json` scripts when they exist (for example `check-types` instead of raw `tsc --noEmit`), unless the script is clearly unsuitable for the requested task.
